WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:04.600
The OnePlus 7 Pro is a really nice device,
and with a starting price that sounded surprisingly

00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:07.569
low after all of its features and specs were
revealed.

00:00:07.569 --> 00:00:11.740
Its got a beautiful super smooth display,
dual stereo speakers, and top of the line

00:00:11.740 --> 00:00:16.330
performance specs, but after spending a week
with it, I have to say I wouldn’t buy it.

00:00:16.330 --> 00:00:20.850
Now don’t get me wrong, it's not a bad phone
by any means, in fact, its industry-leading

00:00:20.850 --> 00:00:25.851
in multiple areas, but it's not without its
flaws, and in many areas its just good, not

00:00:25.851 --> 00:00:26.851
great.

00:00:26.851 --> 00:00:30.190
I’ll let you know exactly what those are
including which phone I’d buy instead, but

00:00:30.190 --> 00:00:31.900
first, let's talk about what they got right.

00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:35.899
The exterior design not only looks nice, but
feels very premium.

00:00:35.899 --> 00:00:40.510
Aluminum sandwiched by curved gorilla glass,
Subtle logo and text on the back, perfectly

00:00:40.510 --> 00:00:45.000
located buttons, the same triple mute switch
that I love, and hefty weight that adds to

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:46.000
the premium feel.

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:49.730
We don’t have waterproofing rating but various
videos and breakdowns have shown it's up to

00:00:49.730 --> 00:00:51.570
the task so I wouldn’t worry.

00:00:51.570 --> 00:00:56.819
The center of attention is the massive curved
OLED display coming in at 6.7 inches.

00:00:56.819 --> 00:01:00.739
It's bright, has great color accuracy, and
is super sharp.

00:01:00.739 --> 00:01:04.869
As you can see there isn’t any kinda notch
or cutout and at the same time we have very

00:01:04.869 --> 00:01:06.210
slim bezels.

00:01:06.210 --> 00:01:10.659
Not only that, but the 90hz refresh rate paired
with great software makes using it the most

00:01:10.659 --> 00:01:13.530
smooth experience I’ve ever had on a smartphone.

00:01:13.530 --> 00:01:17.799
To make this fullscreen experience possible
OnePlus designed a motorized front facing

00:01:17.799 --> 00:01:21.530
camera and I think this is probably the best
solution for the notch issue.

00:01:21.530 --> 00:01:25.729
They showed it holding over 50lbs of weight
which is crazy, and say it's rated for over

00:01:25.729 --> 00:01:30.899
300,000 actuations, so I don’t think durability
should be an issue but only time will tell.

00:01:30.899 --> 00:01:36.119
Inside of that popup is a really good 16MP
F2 selfie camera, and on the back we have

00:01:36.119 --> 00:01:40.840
3 more in a layout that's been very popular
recently, a standard, a telephoto, and an

00:01:40.840 --> 00:01:41.909
ultrawide.

00:01:41.909 --> 00:01:47.680
OnePlus chose to go with a 48MP main camera
instead of Apples and Samsungs 12MP, and on

00:01:47.680 --> 00:01:55.380
the telephoto an 8MP 3x zoom, which was found
to actually be a 13MP 2.2 that they crop into

00:01:55.380 --> 00:02:00.229
which makes sense since the zoomed images
don't look much better than 2x systems cropped

00:02:00.229 --> 00:02:01.229
in digitally.

00:02:01.229 --> 00:02:05.740
The photo and video capabilities are much
better than any previous device and very good

00:02:05.740 --> 00:02:08.550
overall, but is it enough to take on the flagships?

00:02:08.550 --> 00:02:10.140
No, not really.

00:02:10.140 --> 00:02:12.730
Many images look fantastic but it's inconsistent.

00:02:12.730 --> 00:02:16.410
Some shots turn out perfect while many others
have highlights pulled down too much, and

00:02:16.410 --> 00:02:18.630
other having too much contrast or denoising.

00:02:18.630 --> 00:02:22.850
The same inconsistency shows up in the video
as well, and some things are just missing

00:02:22.850 --> 00:02:25.090
like video recording with a wide angle.

00:02:25.090 --> 00:02:30.310
The sensors are great but the software still
needs tweaking which means OnePlus can improve

00:02:30.310 --> 00:02:34.870
it, but at this time the 7 Pro can’t compare
with the S10+ or XS Max.

00:02:34.870 --> 00:02:38.480
If you want to see a detailed comparison I’ll
link it after the video.

00:02:38.480 --> 00:02:43.150
Although the camera needs work, I have to
say it again, OnePlus has the best Android

00:02:43.150 --> 00:02:44.150
Software.

00:02:44.150 --> 00:02:49.480
The icons, shortcuts, keyboard, and quick
animations are better than even stock android

00:02:49.480 --> 00:02:52.310
and we also finally have an out of the box
screen recorder on an Android.

00:02:52.310 --> 00:02:55.660
This wouldn’t be possible without great
hardware and in typical OnePlus fashion we

00:02:55.660 --> 00:03:02.240
have a flagship Snapdragon 855 processor with
a ton of ram, up to 12GB in fact and OnePlus

00:03:02.240 --> 00:03:06.830
can actually make use of that with their RAM
Boost feature that preloads software.

00:03:06.830 --> 00:03:11.420
Add in brand new UFS 3 storage which in the
real world doubles read and write speed, and

00:03:11.420 --> 00:03:15.500
you have a crazy fast phone that loads apps
noticeably faster than the competition.

00:03:15.500 --> 00:03:21.160
The optical fingerprint sensor, in my opinion,
is now just as good as a physical one, and

00:03:21.160 --> 00:03:24.950
definitely better than Samsungs ultrasonic.

00:03:24.950 --> 00:03:28.900
So that's a bunch of great features of the
OnePlus 7 Pro, and when you pair that with

00:03:28.900 --> 00:03:36.310
a $700 price tag for the model most will likely
choose, the 8GB RAM 256GB storage I’m using,

00:03:36.310 --> 00:03:40.240
the value proposition is incredible, so why
wouldn’t I buy one?

00:03:40.240 --> 00:03:46.520
The biggest culprit is the S10+ and the fact
that just two months later its been deeply

00:03:46.520 --> 00:03:52.910
discounted on multiple websites bringing it
down from the $1000 I paid, to as low as $700

00:03:52.910 --> 00:03:57.040
for an international model or just a bit more
for a Snapdragon version.

00:03:57.040 --> 00:04:00.740
That is just crazy, I’ll leave some link
in the video description for some of the deals

00:04:00.740 --> 00:04:01.740
I’ve found.

00:04:01.740 --> 00:04:06.130
If the OnePlus 7 Pro was released half a year
ago it would have destroyed the market, or

00:04:06.130 --> 00:04:11.610
if the S10+ stayed at $300 more the 7 Pro
would be a no brainer, but with Samsungs flagship

00:04:11.610 --> 00:04:15.790
being available so close in price the OnePlus
is hard to recommend for most.

00:04:15.790 --> 00:04:20.320
When we compare them side by side the OnePlus
falls behind in too many areas.

00:04:20.320 --> 00:04:24.250
The battery charger is super fast but you
have to use both their proprietary charger

00:04:24.250 --> 00:04:29.780
and cable, and the 4000MAh battery is large
but the 90hz display drains the battery so

00:04:29.780 --> 00:04:34.450
much that I couldn’t ever get a full day
of use like I can with the S10+ which still

00:04:34.450 --> 00:04:37.010
has 10-15% remaining.

00:04:37.010 --> 00:04:40.250
To make matters worse we still don’t have
wireless charging so you can’t leave it

00:04:40.250 --> 00:04:42.120
on a stand to top off throughout the day.

00:04:42.120 --> 00:04:47.380
I understood it at $530, but I think at this
price point, paired with the “Pro” name

00:04:47.380 --> 00:04:50.800
and high battery drain, OnePlus needed to
include it.

00:04:50.800 --> 00:04:53.120
The display is nice, but it also can’t compete.

00:04:53.120 --> 00:04:58.020
Samsungs is quite a bit brighter and HDR videos
look much better on the S10, and the same

00:04:58.020 --> 00:05:03.411
thing goes for speakers, the S10+ blows the
OnePlus 7 Pro’s average stereo pair way

00:05:03.411 --> 00:05:20.410
in sound quality and volume.

00:05:20.410 --> 00:05:24.460
It's nice not having a cutout but the curved
portion of the screen starts bending much

00:05:24.460 --> 00:05:27.000
earlier so reflections are a bigger issue.

00:05:27.000 --> 00:05:31.150
If you like listening to music and watching
videos on your phone the S10 is definitely

00:05:31.150 --> 00:05:32.150
ahead.

00:05:32.150 --> 00:05:37.620
The S10’s camera quality is much more consistent
and overall better in both photos and video,

00:05:37.620 --> 00:05:42.030
especially for the ultrawide lens where the
photos are far ahead because of processing,

00:05:42.030 --> 00:05:49.060
are wider, and allow for video recording with
a cool super steady feature.

00:05:49.060 --> 00:05:54.850
You do get 128GB of slower but still fast
storage as the base but the SD card slot will

00:05:54.850 --> 00:06:01.260
accept up to another 512, and for those that
use wired headphone we still have a headphone

00:06:01.260 --> 00:06:02.260
jack.

00:06:02.260 --> 00:06:05.630
And I’m leaving my biggest to complaint
for last, and that the size and weight.

00:06:05.630 --> 00:06:10.120
I never thought I’d say it but this smartphone
screen is just too big.

00:06:10.120 --> 00:06:16.590
I love the large screens but 6.7” paired
with 206 grams means that in some of my pants

00:06:16.590 --> 00:06:18.030
it actually sticks out of the pocket.

00:06:18.030 --> 00:06:22.340
My hands were noticeably more tired when watching
youtube for a while and playing games compared

00:06:22.340 --> 00:06:27.740
to the S10+ which is smaller, thinner, and
about 20% lighter while still having a large

00:06:27.740 --> 00:06:29.260
6.4” display.

00:06:29.260 --> 00:06:33.180
In the real world, this phone will be too
large for most people, and that's before adding

00:06:33.180 --> 00:06:34.180
a case.

00:06:34.180 --> 00:06:38.620
The OnePlus 7 Pro is a really nice phone that
leads in multiple areas but to achieve that

00:06:38.620 --> 00:06:40.310
they had to raise the cost.

00:06:40.310 --> 00:06:44.340
At the same time, competition has really upped
its game and is still ahead like they were

00:06:44.340 --> 00:06:45.639
in previous years, but now the price tags
are closer together.

00:06:45.639 --> 00:06:52.449
If your priority is a super smooth experience
both with software and display, and fast specs

00:06:52.449 --> 00:06:55.830
for a great gaming experience it could still
make sense, but for most people, if you can

00:06:55.830 --> 00:07:19.440
spend just a bit more, I think the S10+ is
a better choice.

